1
00:00:02,920 --> 00:00:04,740
Long ago, Gold Roger,

2
00:00:04,960 --> 00:00:08,457
the King of Pirates, obtained
everything the world had to offer,

3
00:00:08,540 --> 00:00:11,940
and his dying roads drove
countless souls to the seas.

4
00:00:12,380 --> 00:00:13,680
You want my treasure?

5
00:00:13,900 --> 00:00:15,020
You can have it!

6
00:00:15,200 --> 00:00:17,700
I left everything in one place.

7
00:00:17,920 --> 00:00:19,940
Now you just have to find it!

8
00:00:20,240 --> 00:00:21,800
And thus a new age began.

9
00:00:22,080 --> 00:00:25,380
This is the time known
as the Great Pirate Era!

10
00:00:27,360 --> 00:00:30,680
Oh, I'm done playing
through with the waiting,

11
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:35,100
either will I'm feeling alive,
look out below, wake up sunshine,

12
00:00:35,520 --> 00:00:37,280
here we go.

13
00:00:38,900 --> 00:00:42,920
Raise your flag up high,
hail a brand new dawn.

14
00:00:44,700 --> 00:00:49,297
Blaze across the sky, time
to journey on, on your mark.

15
00:00:49,380 --> 00:00:51,137
Come aboard with me.

16
00:00:51,220 --> 00:00:53,180
We're on Earth, a legendary!.

17
00:00:54,160 --> 00:00:55,977
If you can show your breath?

18
00:00:56,060 --> 00:00:57,860
Then we'll make some waves!.

19
00:00:58,860 --> 00:01:00,377
We run our daunted!.

20
00:01:00,460 --> 00:01:01,637
Ain't no beginners!.

21
00:01:01,720 --> 00:01:03,017
Cause if you're wanted?

22
00:01:03,100 --> 00:01:04,377
Then you're a winner!.

23
00:01:04,460 --> 00:01:06,897
For we are on the cruise!.

24
00:01:06,980 --> 00:01:09,860
And freedom is the only rule!.

25
00:01:10,760 --> 00:01:12,277
Fearless night and day!.

26
00:01:12,360 --> 00:01:14,200
Cause that's just our way!.

27
00:01:15,880 --> 00:01:17,197
Find one piece!.

28
00:01:17,280 --> 00:01:18,557
I'll be the first!.

29
00:01:18,640 --> 00:01:20,377
I've heard it be so bad just at first!.

30
00:01:20,460 --> 00:01:21,937
It's all this real!.

31
00:01:22,020 --> 00:01:26,360
It must be cause my hand's on a wheel!.

32
00:01:27,000 --> 00:01:29,417
I'm done playing, feel it's waiting!.

33
00:01:29,500 --> 00:01:31,457
In the world I'm feeling alive!.

34
00:01:31,540 --> 00:01:33,237
But I'll be loud!.

35
00:01:33,320 --> 00:01:37,100
Wake up sunshine, here we go!.

36
00:01:38,660 --> 00:01:40,500
We have come so far!.

37
00:01:41,520 --> 00:01:44,357
Gotta make it to the end!.

38
00:01:44,440 --> 00:01:47,677
Whatever danger we find,
no one ever left behind!.

39
00:01:47,760 --> 00:01:51,820
I've always got your back, my friend!.

40
00:01:52,620 --> 00:01:55,457
Sail on shoreward, keep marching forward!.

41
00:01:55,540 --> 00:01:59,117
Dreaming from the very first
day, I'd make my name!.

42
00:01:59,200 --> 00:02:03,300
And don't you know that
dream hasn't changed!.

43
00:02:03,920 --> 00:02:06,317
I'm done playing through with the wave!.

44
00:02:06,400 --> 00:02:09,660
In the world I'm feeling
alive, look out below!.

45
00:02:10,480 --> 00:02:13,080
Wake up, sunshine!.

46
00:02:14,480 --> 00:02:17,040
Wake up, sunshine!.

47
00:02:18,800 --> 00:02:23,560
Wake up, sunshine, here we go!.

48
00:02:27,320 --> 00:02:28,560
We go!.

49
00:02:30,720 --> 00:02:32,540
In the decade that followed,

50
00:02:32,820 --> 00:02:36,477
the remaining members of the royal
family, including the king himself,?

51
00:02:36,560 --> 00:02:37,697
rarely left the palace,

52
00:02:37,780 --> 00:02:41,545
but chose to speak to the nation
through their monitors instead.

53
00:02:42,340 --> 00:02:46,260
And all the while, the islander's
signature steadily replenished.

54
00:02:47,340 --> 00:02:48,760
So there you have it.

55
00:02:49,080 --> 00:02:52,727
That's how we spent the past 16
years fighting discrimination.

56
00:02:52,980 --> 00:02:56,800
And that's how the Fishman
Pirates were formed and divided.

57
00:02:59,720 --> 00:03:03,249
There's no denying the awful
things Arlong did to your home.

58
00:03:03,700 --> 00:03:08,120
Even so, at one time, he
was like a brother to me.

59
00:03:12,200 --> 00:03:17,577
When we received news of his violent actions
we took it upon ourselves to stop him.

60
00:03:17,660 --> 00:03:20,900
But he always managed to
dodge any real consequence.

61
00:03:21,620 --> 00:03:26,149
He hid his actions from the navy by
bribing any soldiers that he came across.

62
00:03:26,600 --> 00:03:32,100
I let him live and in failing to stop
him I too share the guilt for his crimes.

63
00:03:32,740 --> 00:03:35,640
If you're so sorry kill yourself.

64
00:03:36,940 --> 00:03:42,377
Sanji take responsibility pay with your
life for the suffering that you caused her.

65
00:03:42,460 --> 00:03:47,157
Give her peace that's
enough Sanji what are you

66
00:03:47,240 --> 00:03:49,997
serious Nami how could
you excuse the things they

67
00:03:50,080 --> 00:03:52,477
Did to you I'll never
excuse what Arlong did

68
00:03:52,560 --> 00:03:55,617
but Jinbei he never meant
for anyone to get hurt.

69
00:03:55,700 --> 00:04:01,020
I will accept any punishment if you
wish for me to take my own life drop it.

70
00:04:02,800 --> 00:04:03,917
Look it's okay.

71
00:04:04,000 --> 00:04:06,180
The only one I hate is Arlong.

72
00:04:11,640 --> 00:04:16,346
Believe me I'm relieved to hear you're
not the mastermind of the Arlong Pirates.

73
00:04:16,480 --> 00:04:20,186
And you're a friend of Luffy's
which tells me plenty about you.

74
00:04:20,480 --> 00:04:21,310
I won't lie.

75
00:04:21,393 --> 00:04:24,320
The Arlong Pirates made
my life a living hell.

76
00:04:25,240 --> 00:04:29,887
But you know if it wasn't for that
nightmare I never would have met my friends.

77
00:04:30,360 --> 00:04:35,937
That awful time made me who I am I can't

78
00:04:36,020 --> 00:04:38,373
hate you just because you're a fish man.

79
00:04:39,600 --> 00:04:43,620
So you you don't get to pity
me just because of my past.

80
00:04:45,460 --> 00:04:49,220
I'm fine with my past because
I'm happy in the present.

81
00:04:53,160 --> 00:04:58,720
It doesn't matter who did
this to me don't become angry.

82
00:04:59,320 --> 00:05:00,800
not on my behalf.

83
00:05:02,940 --> 00:05:05,411
Please you can't tell anyone on the island

84
00:05:06,000 --> 00:05:07,797
the tragedy that we've endured?

85
00:05:07,880 --> 00:05:10,400
and our hatred must die with us.

86
00:05:11,880 --> 00:05:13,340
I wouldn't dwell on it.

87
00:05:13,580 --> 00:05:15,137
There's nothing you could have done.

88
00:05:15,220 --> 00:05:18,220
You've known each other
since childhood, after all.

89
00:05:18,520 --> 00:05:22,696
Like him or not, he's still like a
brother to you and you're no killer.

90
00:05:29,680 --> 00:05:32,680
I don't deserve to be treated so kindly.

91
00:05:35,380 --> 00:05:37,220
You have my gratitude.

92
00:05:42,260 --> 00:05:43,760
You... Nami.

93
00:05:49,920 --> 00:05:51,700
You're a good man, Jinpei.

94
00:05:53,840 --> 00:05:56,537
I know how hard it is to be a big brother.

95
00:05:56,620 --> 00:05:59,180
You're a hell of a guy, Jinbei!

96
00:06:00,700 --> 00:06:02,237
That whole story?

97
00:06:02,320 --> 00:06:04,357
I like them all so much!

98
00:06:04,440 --> 00:06:06,097
Tiger and Odashime!

99
00:06:06,180 --> 00:06:07,760
Shut your mouth, Franky!

100
00:06:09,640 --> 00:06:12,320
He must have been carrying so much pain.

101
00:06:23,400 --> 00:06:24,230
Luffy?

102
00:06:28,420 --> 00:06:29,250
What?

103
00:06:29,400 --> 00:06:30,230
What?

104
00:06:31,620 --> 00:06:33,260
Moron. Wake up!

105
00:06:36,800 --> 00:06:38,500
I didn't need that nap.

106
00:06:39,940 --> 00:06:40,770
So?

107
00:06:41,180 --> 00:06:42,517
Jinbei, what did the queen?

108
00:06:42,600 --> 00:06:44,597
end up doing to that beast you got?

109
00:06:44,680 --> 00:06:45,800
Are you for real?

110
00:06:46,000 --> 00:06:48,697
You mean you fell asleep at the
very beginning of the story?

111
00:06:48,780 --> 00:06:49,610
Did I miss it all?

112
00:06:49,693 --> 00:06:50,523
You did!

113
00:06:51,560 --> 00:06:52,619
Shirahoshi, right?

114
00:06:52,780 --> 00:06:53,839
You gonna be okay?

115
00:06:54,920 --> 00:06:55,750
Nami-chin!

116
00:06:55,840 --> 00:06:56,760
She's royalty!

117
00:06:57,060 --> 00:06:58,660
Don't be so casual, please!

118
00:07:00,440 --> 00:07:02,537
Oh, forgive me for being so emotional.

119
00:07:02,620 --> 00:07:05,855
It's difficult not to cry
when I think about my mother.

120
00:07:06,000 --> 00:07:08,353
She sounds like she was quite the woman.

121
00:07:10,040 --> 00:07:10,870
Yes.

122
00:07:12,180 --> 00:07:14,768
It's a real pleasure
to meet you, Nami-chin.

123
00:07:15,320 --> 00:07:16,200
No, princess!

124
00:07:16,480 --> 00:07:20,957
Nami-chin is just a silly nickname I gave
her, so it's just plain Nami, no chin!

125
00:07:21,040 --> 00:07:21,960
Excuse me,

126
00:07:22,380 --> 00:07:24,617
perhaps it's a bit
forward of me to say this,

127
00:07:24,700 --> 00:07:27,697
but even though we just met,
I feel a connection to you,

128
00:07:27,780 --> 00:07:30,133
like we've been friends for a long time.

129
00:07:30,760 --> 00:07:31,590
Oh yeah?

130
00:07:31,673 --> 00:07:34,633
Well, we've both been through
some similar rough patches.

131
00:07:39,320 --> 00:07:43,460
Excuse me, I just lost track of time.

132
00:07:43,800 --> 00:07:47,153
I need to know what the
situation is at the Ryugu Palace.

133
00:07:47,600 --> 00:07:49,718
Just to confirm what you've told me,

134
00:07:49,940 --> 00:07:53,637
Heart and his crew have taken the
King and the Palace Guards captive.

135
00:07:53,720 --> 00:07:57,957
Apart from that, you're not sure what
happened to three members of your crew.

136
00:07:58,040 --> 00:08:00,864
And that's all the
information we have, correct?

137
00:08:01,120 --> 00:08:01,950
You...

138
00:08:02,033 --> 00:08:05,580
Hey, Jinbei, if the siege is
playing out as Heart planned,

139
00:08:06,000 --> 00:08:10,706
there's a good chance the rest of the
country is falling to his forces now, too.

140
00:08:10,900 --> 00:08:11,760
Hold on.

141
00:08:11,980 --> 00:08:14,392
Are you saying you know what his plan is?

142
00:08:14,740 --> 00:08:15,570
To be honest,

143
00:08:15,860 --> 00:08:20,801
I have had my suspicions he was up to
something ever since he retired from the army.

144
00:08:20,980 --> 00:08:24,509
But he was clever enough to
keep the details hidden from me.

145
00:08:25,240 --> 00:08:27,000
Not me, I know.

146
00:08:27,380 --> 00:08:29,240
But first, let me warn you.

147
00:08:29,700 --> 00:08:32,347
Heart hates humans even
more than Arlong did.

148
00:08:32,560 --> 00:08:34,697
The only thing driving him is resentment.

149
00:08:34,780 --> 00:08:36,837
He talks about rebuilding the kingdom,

150
00:08:36,920 --> 00:08:40,391
but all he really wants to do
is cause suffering to humans.

151
00:08:40,540 --> 00:08:45,481
And to prove my point, you'll see there's
one big difference between him and Arlong.

152
00:08:46,200 --> 00:08:48,537
Arlong had no problem with killing humans,

153
00:08:48,620 --> 00:08:51,796
but the one thing he'd never
do is hurt other fishmen.

154
00:08:52,960 --> 00:08:54,640
Heart, he doesn't care.

155
00:08:55,200 --> 00:08:59,376
He'll also turn his fury against
fishmen who are sympathetic to humans.

156
00:08:59,980 --> 00:09:02,260
He'll cut down anyone in his way.

157
00:09:03,160 --> 00:09:05,937
The World Summit is set
to take place again soon,

158
00:09:06,020 --> 00:09:08,097
but a lot's changed in
the last four years.

159
00:09:08,180 --> 00:09:11,100
For the first time since Odohime's death,

160
00:09:11,420 --> 00:09:14,997
they've actually gathered enough
signatures for King Neptune to

161
00:09:15,080 --> 00:09:19,021
speak at the summit about relocating
Fishman Island to the surface.

162
00:09:20,840 --> 00:09:21,670
Hmm.

163
00:09:21,753 --> 00:09:22,583
I see.

164
00:09:22,666 --> 00:09:25,880
Then Hortius seized the
palace just for that? I wish.

165
00:09:26,160 --> 00:09:28,631
No, I'm afraid it's a lot worse than that.

166
00:09:35,100 --> 00:09:35,930
What?

167
00:09:36,013 --> 00:09:36,880
What is that?

168
00:09:39,860 --> 00:09:41,040
It's huge!

169
00:09:41,480 --> 00:09:42,656
Think it's that big?

170
00:09:43,120 --> 00:09:44,060
What the?

171
00:09:44,280 --> 00:09:46,700
It's a video transponder snail.

172
00:09:47,060 --> 00:09:48,531
What's it doing out here?

173
00:09:50,720 --> 00:09:52,640
Look! It's activated!

174
00:09:53,860 --> 00:09:55,400
Oh yeah, it's projecting!

175
00:09:55,740 --> 00:09:56,620
On the bubble!

176
00:09:59,180 --> 00:10:00,840
Hmm, I thought so.

177
00:10:03,800 --> 00:10:04,877
It's him.

178
00:10:04,960 --> 00:10:06,440
What's up?

179
00:10:06,900 --> 00:10:08,220
You know that guy?

180
00:10:08,640 --> 00:10:09,600
That's Heart.

181
00:10:09,920 --> 00:10:11,380
This can't be good.

182
00:10:12,220 --> 00:10:14,460
He found us? Hodges!

183
00:10:15,300 --> 00:10:18,680
Hello there, people of Fishman Island.

184
00:10:19,720 --> 00:10:21,240
Am I coming through?

185
00:10:22,280 --> 00:10:23,320
Well then,

186
00:10:23,660 --> 00:10:28,131
for those of you who don't know, I'm
the captain of the new Fishman Pirates.

187
00:10:28,780 --> 00:10:31,920
My name is Heart Jones!

188
00:10:33,340 --> 00:10:35,300
Come on! Next!

189
00:10:37,100 --> 00:10:37,930
Next!

190
00:10:42,040 --> 00:10:42,870
Next!

191
00:10:48,800 --> 00:10:50,420
You won't step on it!

192
00:10:54,620 --> 00:10:56,973
I'm sure Queen Otohime would forgive us.

193
00:10:57,140 --> 00:10:59,100
If I refused, it would kill me.

194
00:10:59,460 --> 00:11:01,257
I can't believe this is happening.

195
00:11:01,340 --> 00:11:02,757
I'm sorry, Queen Otohime.

196
00:11:02,840 --> 00:11:04,140
I don't want to.

197
00:11:04,340 --> 00:11:05,420
There you go.

198
00:11:06,100 --> 00:11:06,930
Next.

199
00:11:10,760 --> 00:11:11,800
How boring.

200
00:11:11,920 --> 00:11:13,744
No one's even trying to resist.

201
00:11:15,000 --> 00:11:18,059
People are stomping on her
without a second thought.

202
00:11:18,420 --> 00:11:19,400
Hey, Drum.

203
00:11:19,760 --> 00:11:21,217
You've got to come see this quick.

204
00:11:21,300 --> 00:11:23,182
Captain Horty's live on the air.

205
00:11:27,140 --> 00:11:30,120
So he's the one behind
all this. The bastard.

206
00:11:30,400 --> 00:11:33,277
Why does he want us to
stuff on the queen so bad?

207
00:11:33,360 --> 00:11:34,340
Wait, that guy?

208
00:11:34,520 --> 00:11:36,717
Wasn't he also the soldier from the plaza?

209
00:11:36,800 --> 00:11:39,094
He killed Otsuhime's assassin that day.

210
00:11:39,460 --> 00:11:40,300
That's right.

211
00:11:40,500 --> 00:11:42,960
His name is Heart Jones. The same guy.

212
00:11:43,200 --> 00:11:45,977
Why would one of that team
soldiers do such a thing?

213
00:11:46,060 --> 00:11:50,001
There's something every citizen of
the Ryugu kingdom needs to know.

214
00:11:52,360 --> 00:11:55,160
This will be destroyed. And quickly.

215
00:11:55,580 --> 00:11:57,560
We'll rebuild it from scratch.

216
00:11:57,760 --> 00:11:59,117
But with a new king.

217
00:11:59,200 --> 00:12:00,160
Like me.

218
00:12:11,380 --> 00:12:12,777
What's he talking about?

219
00:12:12,860 --> 00:12:15,217
Who does he think he is? Screw you!

220
00:12:15,300 --> 00:12:16,277
This is crazy!

221
00:12:16,360 --> 00:12:18,357
Where is this broadcast even coming from?

222
00:12:18,440 --> 00:12:19,417
King Neptune?

223
00:12:19,500 --> 00:12:20,330
Is he okay?

224
00:12:20,413 --> 00:12:23,037
The Straw Hat supposedly
took over the palace.

225
00:12:23,120 --> 00:12:24,617
Do you think they're his allies?

226
00:12:24,700 --> 00:12:26,737
Nothing makes sense anymore!

227
00:12:26,820 --> 00:12:29,600
I will usher in a new era for?

228
00:12:30,160 --> 00:12:30,990
Fishman Island.

229
00:12:31,073 --> 00:12:34,017
For starters, we'll end all
friendly relations with humans.

230
00:12:34,100 --> 00:12:35,880
In place of the sympathizers,

231
00:12:36,140 --> 00:12:39,905
those loyal to our cause will
move in from the Fishman District.

232
00:12:40,080 --> 00:12:41,577
They hate humans too.

233
00:12:41,660 --> 00:12:43,457
And will do whatever it takes to?

234
00:12:43,540 --> 00:12:44,957
rid this country of them.

235
00:12:45,040 --> 00:12:47,060
So treat them with respect.

236
00:12:47,640 --> 00:12:49,760
Is he serious? New residents?

237
00:12:50,160 --> 00:12:54,278
He's just gonna let all these criminals
roam free through our kingdom?

238
00:12:56,080 --> 00:12:58,340
You still love her, don't you?

239
00:12:59,040 --> 00:13:01,460
Otohime, our most cherished queen.

240
00:13:02,220 --> 00:13:05,117
She was indeed selfless
and worked tirelessly

241
00:13:05,200 --> 00:13:07,457
to build a bridge between
fishmen and humans.

242
00:13:07,540 --> 00:13:09,577
I do respect her spirit.

243
00:13:09,660 --> 00:13:12,420
But have you forgotten
the end of her tale?

244
00:13:12,660 --> 00:13:16,857
She was killed by a no-man Even if you
approach them with a pure heart and

245
00:13:16,940 --> 00:13:21,337
kind intentions They'll just take
advantage of you and leave you in the dirt

246
00:13:21,420 --> 00:13:23,920
We have to wake up, can't you see?

247
00:13:26,760 --> 00:13:27,590
Woody

248
00:13:28,060 --> 00:13:31,580
Sorry, but the royal family's
been duping you for years.

249
00:13:32,000 --> 00:13:34,412
If we follow them, we'll face extinction.

250
00:13:35,120 --> 00:13:38,780
As long as humans exist, the
Skull of Harmony is unattainable.

251
00:13:39,220 --> 00:13:42,691
It's a pipe dream that's been
perpetuated for far too long.

252
00:13:43,020 --> 00:13:44,000
Stop it.

253
00:13:44,240 --> 00:13:45,240
See for yourself.

254
00:13:48,300 --> 00:13:49,560
They have father.

255
00:13:49,980 --> 00:13:51,820
How could they? Father!

256
00:13:52,680 --> 00:13:53,780
Not the king.

257
00:13:54,500 --> 00:13:56,617
King Neptune got old.

258
00:13:56,700 --> 00:13:58,240
It happens to everyone.

259
00:13:59,300 --> 00:14:02,377
The only way to advance is
to eliminate the old god,

260
00:14:02,460 --> 00:14:04,519
so they won't hold us back anymore.

261
00:14:06,960 --> 00:14:07,790
Huh.

262
00:14:07,873 --> 00:14:10,217
When you think about it, this
mess is kind of our fault.

263
00:14:10,300 --> 00:14:13,006
If we hadn't shown up,
the king might be fine.

264
00:14:13,720 --> 00:14:15,320
More like Zoro's fault.

265
00:14:15,580 --> 00:14:17,937
What in the world did
you do at the palace?

266
00:14:18,020 --> 00:14:19,540
Jinbei, wait! Calm down!

267
00:14:19,780 --> 00:14:22,817
A bunch of Neptune soldiers attacked
Namichin and her friends first!

268
00:14:22,900 --> 00:14:25,429
They were just trying
to defend themselves!

269
00:14:45,460 --> 00:14:47,940
As you may have figured out by now,

270
00:14:48,220 --> 00:14:52,700
I am at the Ryugu Palace, and there's
something else I want to show you.

271
00:14:53,940 --> 00:14:56,820
This here is from the nobles.

272
00:14:57,060 --> 00:14:59,119
The queen risked her life for this.

273
00:15:01,080 --> 00:15:03,800
Ten years ago, that is.

274
00:15:05,480 --> 00:15:08,260
If I destroy this letter, it's over.

275
00:15:08,540 --> 00:15:10,069
You won't get another one.

276
00:15:10,600 --> 00:15:11,880
Along with that,

277
00:15:13,540 --> 00:15:15,520
here we have a box

278
00:15:17,200 --> 00:15:20,360
with signatures from
most of Fishman Island.

279
00:15:25,500 --> 00:15:27,860
Frankly, I'm disgusted by the numbers.

280
00:15:28,120 --> 00:15:32,597
Who in their right mind would want to
befriend humans after all they've done?

281
00:15:32,680 --> 00:15:36,080
So, if your name is on
any of these, thank you.

282
00:15:36,240 --> 00:15:37,997
I know who I have to weed out.

283
00:15:38,080 --> 00:15:40,315
My kingdom will be better without you.

284
00:15:41,140 --> 00:15:44,180
And with that in mind,
why don't we get started?

285
00:15:44,400 --> 00:15:45,500
Here's page one.

286
00:15:45,680 --> 00:15:48,200
Enough stepping on pictures. That's true.

287
00:15:48,480 --> 00:15:53,009
It's far too easy to pretend you don't
mind doing it just to save yourselves.

288
00:15:53,360 --> 00:15:55,080
But these signatures,

289
00:15:55,220 --> 00:15:59,937
they give me concrete evidence of who
I can suspect will oppose my rule?

290
00:16:00,020 --> 00:16:02,780
It's like you signed
your own death warrant!

291
00:16:03,400 --> 00:16:08,840
All right then, let's
see who the traitors are.

292
00:16:09,700 --> 00:16:13,320
Also, before I go

293
00:16:16,840 --> 00:16:19,820
Strat, I know you're there

294
00:16:21,020 --> 00:16:24,000
I have something that
may be of interest to you

295
00:16:25,960 --> 00:16:28,677
As you watch from wherever
you are I want you to

296
00:16:28,760 --> 00:16:31,277
know that this is just the
beginning of my revenge!

297
00:16:31,360 --> 00:16:33,060
For what you did to Arlong?

298
00:16:33,740 --> 00:16:34,570
Enjoy.

299
00:16:34,840 --> 00:16:37,220
Oh man, he even captured Zoro?

300
00:16:37,840 --> 00:16:41,440
That's what we get, leaving
them alone But still, all three?

301
00:16:43,660 --> 00:16:45,320
Do it. Right.

302
00:16:46,520 --> 00:16:47,360
Do it.

303
00:16:54,380 --> 00:16:56,580
Oh no, what's this? We're going up.

304
00:16:56,800 --> 00:16:58,500
This can't possibly be good.

305
00:17:03,620 --> 00:17:05,340
Well, yes, now what?

306
00:17:12,700 --> 00:17:13,818
Something's coming.

307
00:17:18,120 --> 00:17:19,200
It's water!

308
00:17:20,740 --> 00:17:26,460
By the time we finish the king's execution,
that room will be completely flooded.

309
00:17:27,160 --> 00:17:30,820
You know the humans can't survive
that, if I'm not mistaken.

310
00:17:31,300 --> 00:17:32,140
Too bad.

311
00:17:33,320 --> 00:17:34,440
Straw Hat, Luffy!

312
00:17:34,680 --> 00:17:35,856
Look at that bounty!

313
00:17:36,220 --> 00:17:37,455
Four hundred million!

314
00:17:37,800 --> 00:17:40,337
The heads of you and your
crewmates will serve as

315
00:17:40,420 --> 00:17:43,137
a perfect warning to any
humans who dare defy us!

316
00:17:43,220 --> 00:17:47,620
But for now, we're tearing
down the old Ryugu kingdom!

317
00:17:52,480 --> 00:17:54,900
We're done with the failures of the past.

318
00:17:55,240 --> 00:17:57,680
This is the time for revolution!

319
00:17:58,280 --> 00:18:00,540
Just three hours, that's all we need.

320
00:18:00,780 --> 00:18:04,015
Fishman Island will take back
its pride in three hours!

321
00:18:04,460 --> 00:18:05,800
Ja-ha-ha-ha-ha!

322
00:18:14,100 --> 00:18:15,440
We can't stay!

323
00:18:31,840 --> 00:18:34,200
We shall stop them!

324
00:18:37,400 --> 00:18:38,500
Hey guys!

325
00:18:38,780 --> 00:18:41,457
This water isn't getting any lower! Oh no!

326
00:18:41,540 --> 00:18:43,780
Oh, I just got dry, too.

327
00:18:44,120 --> 00:18:46,591
Now let's all figure out a way to save me.

328
00:18:47,120 --> 00:18:48,880
Or better yet, save us!

329
00:18:49,140 --> 00:18:52,180
Do you have any ideas?
Any day? I'm thinking.

330
00:18:54,140 --> 00:18:56,300
First, get me out of these chains.

331
00:18:56,680 --> 00:18:57,800
You got it!

332
00:18:58,160 --> 00:19:00,520
Psychic powers, don't fail me now!

333
00:19:00,880 --> 00:19:02,020
Chains come off!

334
00:19:02,300 --> 00:19:03,360
Chains come off!

335
00:19:03,540 --> 00:19:05,117
Your links are getting looser.

336
00:19:05,200 --> 00:19:06,788
The metal's getting weaker.

337
00:19:07,080 --> 00:19:08,280
Chains be gone!

338
00:19:10,120 --> 00:19:10,950
Nothing.

339
00:19:11,540 --> 00:19:12,640
Well, we're stuck.

340
00:19:12,920 --> 00:19:13,957
Nice knowing you guys.

341
00:19:14,040 --> 00:19:15,687
I still can't stop laughing.

342
00:19:16,180 --> 00:19:19,317
Did you see the look on those
fishmen's faces when I stood up?

343
00:19:19,400 --> 00:19:20,230
Priceless.

344
00:19:28,940 --> 00:19:31,240
Poor guy was probably adrift at sea.

345
00:19:31,540 --> 00:19:33,397
I can't help but feel sorry for him.

346
00:19:33,480 --> 00:19:35,715
It looks like he died a long time ago.

347
00:19:36,040 --> 00:19:36,870
Rackle!

348
00:19:39,720 --> 00:19:41,220
I did die.

349
00:19:41,540 --> 00:19:46,897
He's alive somewhat well I may
do at least the name's brook

350
00:19:46,980 --> 00:19:50,377
we're all gonna die we wouldn't
have gotten caught if it

351
00:19:50,460 --> 00:19:54,377
weren't for you please help
they're killing me wait never

352
00:19:54,460 --> 00:20:00,157
mind you're killing me too well
at least nami and the others

353
00:20:00,240 --> 00:20:03,697
escaped soon luffy and the
rest of the crew will come

354
00:20:03,780 --> 00:20:07,357
get us out of here wishful
thinking what if they don't as

355
00:20:07,440 --> 00:20:11,937
robin would say oh i hope
nami hasn't been eaten by some

356
00:20:12,020 --> 00:20:12,917
deep sea creature

357
00:20:13,000 --> 00:20:20,000
this

358
00:20:30,760 --> 00:20:31,590
poneglyph

359
00:20:31,673 --> 00:20:32,967
is different from the others

360
00:20:33,360 --> 00:20:39,280
let's see it looks like a
letter as well as an apology

361
00:20:40,920 --> 00:20:47,380
but who is this apology for and why
did you engrave it in stone joy boy

362
00:21:03,260 --> 00:21:07,117
hey that's a lot of money
400 million where did

363
00:21:07,200 --> 00:21:10,460
they go up huh no one
cares about your bounty

364
00:21:12,920 --> 00:21:15,197
Obviously, they're using
the others as bait.

365
00:21:15,280 --> 00:21:16,317
Think about it, Luffy.

366
00:21:16,400 --> 00:21:17,576
You're infamous now.

367
00:21:17,720 --> 00:21:20,367
The conflict at Marineford
made sure of that.

368
00:21:20,700 --> 00:21:24,360
Once you surpass 300 million,
it rarely increases again.

369
00:21:28,800 --> 00:21:32,297
Well, anyway, if someone wants
to fight me, I'll fight them.

370
00:21:32,380 --> 00:21:34,260
I beg you, don't act rashly.

371
00:21:36,360 --> 00:21:37,480
They have father.

372
00:21:42,040 --> 00:21:43,880
My father needs me!

373
00:21:44,260 --> 00:21:45,360
I have to help!

374
00:21:45,560 --> 00:21:46,680
I'm coming, Daddy!

375
00:21:48,640 --> 00:21:49,470
Megalo!

376
00:21:53,180 --> 00:21:57,120
I can't just stay here!
Come back! Shura Hachi!

377
00:21:59,880 --> 00:22:01,297
Megalo, don't move!

378
00:22:01,380 --> 00:22:02,760
You could die!

379
00:22:04,360 --> 00:22:07,037
If I don't save father, maybe...

380
00:22:07,120 --> 00:22:11,260
I do understand the urgency,
but please, you must listen.

381
00:22:12,240 --> 00:22:13,070
You...

382
00:22:13,153 --> 00:22:13,983
he's right.

383
00:22:14,280 --> 00:22:16,000
You can't go back right now.

384
00:22:16,480 --> 00:22:17,320
You too?

385
00:22:18,160 --> 00:22:24,660
The one person that Heart is most afraid
of in the Ryugu kingdom is you, princess.

386
00:22:25,120 --> 00:22:25,960
Your power.

387
00:22:28,100 --> 00:22:32,865
Even if Heart does change the island to
suit his needs, you'll still be a threat.

388
00:22:33,120 --> 00:22:37,708
If you summon the sea kings, everything
will come crashing down in an instant.

389
00:22:38,480 --> 00:22:40,637
That's why he took King Neptune hostage,

390
00:22:40,720 --> 00:22:43,600
to neutralize the princess
and to lure her back.

391
00:22:43,860 --> 00:22:48,780
You're saying this whole time, they've
really been after Shirahoshi? You.

392
00:22:49,440 --> 00:22:51,793
Yes, but not in the way you might think.

393
00:22:52,040 --> 00:22:55,077
Heart doesn't want to capture
the princess to use her power.

394
00:22:55,160 --> 00:22:59,454
This may sound cruel, but he'd prefer
a threat like her not exist at all.

395
00:22:59,860 --> 00:23:02,389
That's why he partnered
with Vander Decken.

396
00:23:02,580 --> 00:23:05,580
Deccan is capable of killing
her, plain and simple.

397
00:23:05,740 --> 00:23:08,446
He'll destroy anything
that stands in his way.

398
00:23:09,300 --> 00:23:10,130
Hmm.

399
00:23:10,213 --> 00:23:11,043
That's right.

400
00:23:11,126 --> 00:23:13,457
Heart wants the princess
to rush into the plaza.

401
00:23:13,540 --> 00:23:15,820
There, she would be most vulnerable.

402
00:23:16,200 --> 00:23:20,376
Um, my family has mentioned my power
before, but I'm afraid that's all.

403
00:23:20,500 --> 00:23:23,317
Even if you were to ask me to
communicate with the Sea Kings,

404
00:23:23,400 --> 00:23:24,597
I don't think I could do it.

405
00:23:24,680 --> 00:23:25,510
Not now.

406
00:23:25,593 --> 00:23:29,734
To be honest, I'm not convinced that
I have the power in the first place.

407
00:23:30,080 --> 00:23:34,551
Whether you do or not, Heart has no
qualms with killing you just to be safe.

408
00:23:35,940 --> 00:23:40,477
Therefore, we must not let him find out
that you aren't able to control the power.

409
00:23:40,560 --> 00:23:43,557
The more afraid of you he is,
the better things are for us.

410
00:23:43,640 --> 00:23:44,470
All right.

411
00:23:44,553 --> 00:23:45,640
Are you done? Good.

412
00:23:45,920 --> 00:23:47,000
Then I'm going.

413
00:23:47,960 --> 00:23:50,340
Hey, Shark, take me back to the palace.

414
00:23:51,160 --> 00:23:53,860
I'm leaving the crybaby
with you. That cool?

415
00:23:54,560 --> 00:23:55,390
Hell yeah.

416
00:23:55,660 --> 00:23:57,400
Luffy, I told you to wait.

417
00:23:58,160 --> 00:23:58,990
Huh?

418
00:23:59,073 --> 00:23:59,903
You don't get it.

419
00:24:00,040 --> 00:24:02,197
You people have no
business fighting Heart.

420
00:24:02,280 --> 00:24:03,751
What's the big deal, huh?

421
00:24:04,180 --> 00:24:06,577
We can't fight because
we're humans, is that it?

422
00:24:06,660 --> 00:24:08,477
It doesn't make sense when you two say it.

423
00:24:08,560 --> 00:24:09,877
Quit complicating things.

424
00:24:09,960 --> 00:24:10,790
That's right.

425
00:24:10,873 --> 00:24:12,309
This battle isn't for you.

426
00:24:12,640 --> 00:24:16,464
If you win, the surviving fishmen
will go on hating humans again.

427
00:24:20,680 --> 00:24:22,800
Please, allow me to handle it.

428
00:24:23,400 --> 00:24:24,360
I can't.

429
00:24:24,580 --> 00:24:26,404
Not when my crew is in trouble.

430
00:24:27,020 --> 00:24:28,497
It's not that I don't trust you.

431
00:24:28,580 --> 00:24:30,639
This fight is personal for me, too.

432
00:24:31,540 --> 00:24:32,657
You guys...

433
00:24:32,740 --> 00:24:34,120
They're both right.

434
00:24:38,040 --> 00:24:40,120
Stay out of this. Wait here.

435
00:24:40,380 --> 00:24:41,340
Not a chance.

436
00:24:41,720 --> 00:24:43,260
Such a stubborn fool.

437
00:24:43,420 --> 00:24:44,655
Just shut up already.

438
00:24:44,940 --> 00:24:46,300
I said I'm going.

439
00:24:46,840 --> 00:24:48,000
Stop me if you can.

440
00:24:49,020 --> 00:24:49,850
Lucy.

441
00:24:55,080 --> 00:24:59,457
Since we were allies before, I had
hoped that you would honor my request.

442
00:24:59,540 --> 00:25:02,277
How easily I forget who you are?

443
00:25:02,360 --> 00:25:05,520
Hard-headedness truly
does run in your family.

444
00:25:06,460 --> 00:25:09,980
If you're not going to listen
to me, I have no choice!

445
00:25:20,600 --> 00:25:22,760
Please, you two, try to calm down.

446
00:25:24,320 --> 00:25:25,150
Luffy, Jinbei,

447
00:25:25,233 --> 00:25:28,097
this is no time for you guys to act
like you're going to kill each other.

448
00:25:28,180 --> 00:25:30,957
Get out of my way, I
gotta go save my friends.

449
00:25:31,040 --> 00:25:33,277
And when I'm done, I'm
kicking Horty's ass.

450
00:25:33,360 --> 00:25:35,717
I told you not to get
involved with him, Luffy.

451
00:25:35,800 --> 00:25:38,677
Whoa, hey, surely there's a
better way to work this out?

452
00:25:38,760 --> 00:25:40,277
Yeah, stop it, both of you.

453
00:25:40,360 --> 00:25:43,184
Luffy, please, I don't
want my friends to fight.

454
00:25:44,680 --> 00:25:47,560
Shark, let's go, get
me back to the palace.

455
00:25:48,200 --> 00:25:50,280
You have to go through me first!

456
00:25:50,400 --> 00:25:51,657
Right, fine by me!

457
00:25:51,740 --> 00:25:54,820
Miss Man Caratter, the Shark Brickfish!

458
00:26:03,300 --> 00:26:04,920
What? Oh no!

459
00:26:05,800 --> 00:26:06,960
That looks bad!

460
00:26:15,580 --> 00:26:16,410
That...

461
00:26:16,493 --> 00:26:18,780
That hurt. What? No way.

462
00:26:19,100 --> 00:26:20,117
He's made of rubber.

463
00:26:20,200 --> 00:26:22,157
Attacks like that
shouldn't even work on him.

464
00:26:22,240 --> 00:26:26,280
But this is Fishman Karate, a
form based on manipulating water.

465
00:26:27,240 --> 00:26:29,617
I can send shockwaves through vapor in the

466
00:26:29,700 --> 00:26:32,640
air until they finally
find my target's body.

467
00:26:33,080 --> 00:26:35,657
Seeing as every living
creature is made up of water,

468
00:26:35,740 --> 00:26:38,328
not even a rubber man
can escape the impact.

469
00:26:48,180 --> 00:26:49,160
Bring it!

470
00:26:53,520 --> 00:26:55,940
You shall not pass, Wave!

471
00:26:57,920 --> 00:26:59,020
Second gear!

472
00:26:59,280 --> 00:27:00,380
Now come, come!

473
00:27:12,160 --> 00:27:15,637
After so much training, don't
tell me that's all you've got!

474
00:27:15,720 --> 00:27:16,880
Not a chance!

475
00:27:21,160 --> 00:27:22,580
Enough of that.

476
00:27:25,400 --> 00:27:26,657
You're back.

477
00:27:26,740 --> 00:27:28,797
Hey get out of the way now!

478
00:27:28,880 --> 00:27:30,637
Move it you'll die!

479
00:27:30,720 --> 00:27:33,680
Don't worry I'll save you.

480
00:27:53,020 --> 00:27:54,491
There's no need to fight.

481
00:27:55,660 --> 00:27:59,366
I'm sure you both have your
reasons, but you're friends, right?

482
00:27:59,460 --> 00:28:02,931
Wait, you mean Robin's been in
the forest this entire time?

483
00:28:07,500 --> 00:28:08,977
Well, good luck, you guys!

484
00:28:09,060 --> 00:28:10,178
Wait a damn second!

485
00:28:10,600 --> 00:28:13,497
You're just gonna leave
without explaining or anything?

486
